course: dictionary
lesson: 1667
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the words around it tell you which one the writer means. In «Chocolate melts just below body temperature», chocolate is the sweet brown food, because the sentence is about melting in your mouth.
explain: Chocolate can be a noun, a name for a thing. «A bar of chocolate» and «a box of chocolates» show it being counted. Chocolates is a noun for the sweets themselves, one sweet at a time.
explain: Chocolate can also be an adjective, a word that describes. In «a chocolate cake», chocolate tells you what kind of cake it is. In «chocolate brown», it tells you the colour, which is brown like the food. Swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Chocolate is a sweet brown food made from cocoa beans.
fact: A chocolate is one sweet made of or covered in chocolate.
fact: As an adjective, chocolate means made with chocolate or brown like it, as in «chocolate cake».
fact: Chocolate is made from the seeds of the cocoa tree.
fact: Chocolate melts when warm, which is a change of state in science.
exercise: «Chocolate melts just below body temperature, so it melts in your mouth.» What does chocolate mean here? | *The sweet brown food | A brown colour | A kind of cake | A box of sweets
exercise: «She ate a chocolate from the box.» What is a chocolate in this sentence? | *One sweet made of or covered in chocolate | A cocoa tree | A melted bar | A brown wall
exercise: «We bought a chocolate cake for the party.» What kind of word is chocolate in this sentence? | *An adjective, describing the cake | A number | A verb, an action word | A noun, the name of a food
test: «Chocolate is made from the seeds of the cocoa tree.» Where does chocolate come from? | Strawberry plants | Milk from cows | Potato stems | *Seeds of the cocoa tree
test: Which phrase uses chocolate as an adjective? | *Chocolate brown | A bar of chocolate | Hot chocolate | A box of chocolates
exam: «Chocolate melts in a warm hand and goes hard again in the fridge, but it is still chocolate.» What does this show? | *A change of state, melting and setting again | Chocolate turning into a tree | Chocolate making a cake | Chocolate being counted in a box
